{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 133, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a skip adds a residual path to a deep conv cell, whereas replacing an existing conv/pool there only trades capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-to-output residual skip harms trainability of the stacked network much more than deleting a shallow conv branch on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a weak pooling edge costs little, while removing a 3x3 conv on edge 0 destroys the main deep path through node 1."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 feeds the output only via edge 2 (edge 4 absent), cutting edge 0 removes less useful computation than when node 1 also feeds the output directly."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding conv3x3 to an empty edge 0 revives node 1 and all its downstream edges, a far larger gain than upgrading an existing op there."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a missing edge adds a new branch and capacity, whereas replacing skip/pool/1x1 on edge 1 yields only a marginal change."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pooling on a previously empty edge adds a connection, while overwriting a conv on edge 2 with pooling removes depth and parameters."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op (conv3x3) with parameter-free pooling loses the most accuracy compared with replacing skip, 1x1, or none."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 removed, node 1 is identically zero, so a conv on edge 4 contributes nothing and the edit's benefit vanishes."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on an empty edge 2 links node 1 to node 2 and deepens the cell, while replacing an existing conv3x3 with skip removes capacity."}], "tok": 14844, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", 